---
title: How to sign in
description: The four ways into the Librería de Satoshi campus and which one to pick.
sidebar:
  order: 1
---

The campus lives at [moodle.libreriadesatoshi.com](https://moodle.libreriadesatoshi.com). You have four ways to sign in. All of them lead to the same account and the same courses; pick whichever is most convenient.

| Method | You need | Best if… |
| --- | --- | --- |
| [Nostr](/en/acceso/login-nostr/) | A Nostr browser extension (Alby, nos2x…) | You already use Nostr and want no passwords or email |
| [GitHub](/en/acceso/login-github-google/) | A GitHub account | You are a developer or take the technical courses |
| [Google](/en/acceso/login-github-google/) | A Google account | You want one-click access from any device |
| [Username and password](/en/acceso/crear-cuenta/) | To create an account with your email | You prefer not to link other accounts |

{% aside type="tip" title="Just want a look around?" %}
Some courses allow [guest access](/en/acceso/acceso-invitado/) without an account. It does not save progress or issue certificates, but it lets you read the content.
{% /aside %}

## General steps

{% steps %}

1. Open [moodle.libreriadesatoshi.com/login](https://moodle.libreriadesatoshi.com/login/index.php).

2. At the top you will see the **Nostr**, **GitHub** and **Google** buttons. Below them, the username and password form.

3. Pick your method and follow the prompts. The first time you sign in with Nostr, GitHub or Google, your account is created automatically.

4. You land on your **Dashboard**, with the courses you are enrolled in.

{% /steps %}

## Always use the same method

Each method creates a separate account. If you sign in with Google one day and Nostr the next, you will end up with two accounts and your progress split between them. Pick one and stick to it. If this already happened to you, contact us and we will merge the accounts.

## Common problems

- **I don't remember which method I used.** Try [resetting your password](/en/acceso/recuperar-contrasena/) with your email first. If the system cannot find your account, you most likely signed in with Nostr, GitHub or Google.
- **The Nostr button is missing.** It only shows when the browser has a Nostr extension installed. See [Sign in with Nostr](/en/acceso/login-nostr/).
- **The page says the site is under maintenance.** We are updating the platform. It usually takes a few minutes; try again later.
